 "how": "botcore s84 rolls each bot's Halo 4 armor from the game's own Armory catalog (native/h4f.cpp, the same catalog code as Reach's: 20 slots, each one item with many variants) and equips the picked variant as the game's own equip does (its region / permutation pairs into the appearance block, configuration +0x20: regions at +0x58). Logged live Oct 24 (logs/botcore_logs/botcore_s83.log): slot 0 helmet (86 variants, region 0), slots 1 and 2 the shoulders (81 each, regions 3 and 4), slot 3 the chest (81, region 1), slot 4 the legs (25, region 6; photo: +0x5E changed the legs), slot 5 the forearms (26, region 5). Roll mask 63 = slots 0-5. Checked live: 11 profile bots, 11 different looks (tools/look_check.py --game h4). The armor effect is its own value (appearance +0x40 = configuration +0x60): 0 none (photo: the flames went away), 2 a purple flaming head (photo). MCC added Halo 4's effects: Modern only. Colours and visor (Oct 26 evening, a Forge Island BOT OBSERVER map; found by diffing the local player's configuration before and after setting yellow / green / the reddish Operator visor, then probed bot by bot, tools/look_sheet_aim.py): +0x49 primary, +0x4A secondary (each 0-29: 29 a pale yellow, 30-34 all the same white, the game's fallback past the list), +0x4B visor (0-16, the catalog's 17-variant slot 13: 13 and 16 their own colours, 17 and 20 the same white fallback; the local player's Operator is 12). Laid over the rolled configuration as (offset, value) pairs, both copies (native/h4f.cpp). Halo 4 shipped with colours and visors: both modes. +0x53-0x55 changed with them but moved nothing on the armor (the emblem's, likely): left as the local player's. Original / Modern (Oct 28, docs/HANDOFF_armor_oct28.md): the catalog is Halo 4's own Armory: H4EK's ui/supply_depot.cookie_purchase_globals has the same families with the same counts (helmet 86, shoulders 81 / 81, chest 81, legs 25, forearms 26, visor 17) and its strings name every item: the 42 listed sets and their skins (docs/research/13), the promo ones too (Deadeye, Locus, Scanner, Strider, FOTUS, Mark V, ODST, Prefect, Ricochet, Ricochet HMTM). MCC's unlockdb ids H4_*_FORERUNNER and H4_Helmet_RICOCHET_ALT are Prefect (the tags call it forerunner) and Ricochet HMTM, so the catalog roll is Original as it is. The region bytes are indices of the map's customization table (H4EK globals/player_model_customization: helmet 70 = helmet_spartan_iv_alt, the catalog's variant 1, as logged); the table's only entries no catalog item reaches are the Flood skins (helmet / chest / shoulder 28, arms / legs 8), legs 18 (legs_ecm_b, unused) and helmet 87 helmet_olympus, MCC's H4_Helmet_OLYMPUS: Modern only, the 'mcc' field puts it on 1 bot in 87 by writing +0x58 (both copies) over the roll: NOT SEEN LIVE. The effect byte is the table's 'spartan armor effect selections' index: 0 default, 1 legendary flame, 2 eternal flame (the purple flames seen live), 3 heart attack, 4 pestilence, 5 storm, 6 birthday: Modern rolls 1-6 (only 2 seen). Slots 6+ are not armor: 6-11 the loadout (tactical packages, support upgrades, primary / secondary weapons with their skins, grenades, armor abilities), 13 the visor (the +0x4B byte above), 15 / 16 the emblem, 19 the lobby pose; the emblem's catalog equip writes no bytes, so it is not rolled. Bot editor (Oct 28 night, added since Halo 4 armor and gender could not be set from the profile): every armor slot and the visor can be set by hand, laid over the roll by table index as Olympus is; names from H4EK ui/supply_depot.cookie_purchase_globals (tools/look_names.py). Gender: config +0x4C as Reach (its colours +0x49/+0x4A and visor +0x4B sit where Reach has them), laid only when set by hand, male otherwise: NOT CONFIRMED LIVE. Helmet 87 (helmet_olympus, MCC unlockdb H4_Helmet_OLYMPUS) is the one helmet MCC added to Halo 4; MCC names it KEYSTONE (its only added Halo 4 helmet string; Series 7 Exchange, a Mark VII look in renders, logs/tmp/h4_olympus.png).",
